      "characteristic": "interaction-capability",
      "scope": "holistic",
      "cadence": "triggered",
      "trigger": "pull-request",
      "invocation": "automated",
      "description": "A Playwright test opens each page of the main journeys (PAGES in tests/ux/journeys.ts) and counts, inside the main landmark, the visible links to each target, SVG links included. A target is a page: origin, path and query, a folder and its index.html being one page, and the #fragment left out, so links to different sections of one long page (a manual, a reference) count as one target; that is the point: each is another tab stop to the same page, and a page that needs many is better served by its own table of contents. In-page links (skip links, an error summary's) are left out, and so are links inside a nav: breadcrumbs, a table of contents. It writes the largest count of each page as ux.links.repeated{page=…} and the largest of all as ux.links.repeated.max, and fails on a page over the limit, naming the target. The header, navigation and footer are left out on purpose: the same link in the navigation and once in the text is expected. Bind it with the sensor radical sense playwright tests/ux/links-repeated.spec.ts and the condition ux.links.repeated.max <= {{MAX_LINK_REPEATS}}.\n\nThreshold: ux.links.repeated.max <= {{MAX_LINK_REPEATS}}: on every page of the main journeys, no link target appears more than {{MAX_LINK_REPEATS}} times in the main content outside its navigation (the same link 5 times on a page measures 5 and fails)\n\nTool: Playwright (@playwright/test), measured by radical sense playwright\n\n```ts\n// tests/ux/links-repeated.spec.ts: a plain Playwright test (1.50 or later), or measured with\n//   radical sense playwright tests/ux/links-repeated.spec.ts\nimport { mkdirSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'\nimport { join } from 'node:path'\nimport { expect, test } from '@playwright/test'\nimport { PAGES } from './journeys'   // [{ path: '/' }, { path: '/pricing' }, …]: the main journeys' pages\n\nconst LIMIT = {{MAX_LINK_REPEATS}}   // the decision: how often one target may be linked in a page's main content\n\ntype Measurement = { metric: string; value: number; labels?: Record<string, string> }\n/** Writes what the test measured where radical sense playwright reads it; a plain run writes nothing. */\nfunction writeMetrics(file: string, measurements: Measurement[]): void {\n  const dir = process.env.RADICAL_METRICS_DIR\n  if (!dir) return\n  mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true })\n  writeFileSync(join(dir, file), JSON.stringify({ format: 'radical-metrics', version: 1, source: file, at: new Date().toISOString(), measurements }, null, 1))\n}\n\ntest('no link target repeats in the main content', async ({ page }) => {\n  const found: Array<{ path: string; href: string; times: number }> = []\n  for (const { path } of PAGES) {\n    await page.goto(path)\n    const counts = await page.locator('main').first().evaluate((main) => {\n      const times: Record<string, number> = {}\n      for (const a of main.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement | SVGAElement>('a[href]')) {\n        if (a.closest('nav, [role=\"navigation\"]') || !a.checkVisibility()) continue   // breadcrumbs, tables of contents, hidden links\n        // an SVG link's href is an SVGAnimatedString (links in diagrams)\n        const url = new URL(a instanceof SVGAElement ? a.href.baseVal : a.href, document.baseURI)\n        if (url.origin + url.pathname === location.origin + location.pathname && url.hash) continue   // skip links, error summaries\n        // a target is a page: its #fragment is left out, and a folder and its index.html are one page\n        const target = url.origin + url.pathname.replace(/\\/(index\\.html)?$/, '') + url.search\n        times[target] = (times[target] ?? 0) + 1\n      }\n      return times\n    })\n    const [href, times] = Object.entries(counts).sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1])[0] ?? ['', 0]\n    found.push({ path, href, times })\n  }\n  writeMetrics('links-repeated.json', [\n    ...found.map((p) => ({ metric: 'ux.links.repeated', value: p.times, labels: { page: p.path } })),\n    { metric: 'ux.links.repeated.max', value: Math.max(0, ...found.map((p) => p.times)) },\n  ])\n  for (const p of found) expect.soft(p.times, `${p.path} links to ${p.href} ${p.times} times`).toBeLessThanOrEqual(LIMIT)\n})\n```",
      "hubWhen": {
        "LINK_REPEAT": [
          "limit"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ff-link-texts-unique",
      "type": "fitness-fn",
      "label": "Link names say where they go",
      "x": 1040,
      "y": 650,
      "characteristic": "interaction-capability",
      "scope": "holistic",
      "cadence": "triggered",
      "trigger": "pull-request",
      "invocation": "automated",
      "description": "A Playwright test opens each page of the main journeys and reads every visible link: its accessible name (simplified: aria-labelledby, aria-label, else its text with image alternatives, aria-hidden parts left out), its target, and its context (the text of the table row around it, else of the nearest list item, cell, paragraph, definition or article, so that two \"View\" links in one row meet). SVG links are read too. It writes ux.links.ambiguous{by=name} (names on a page that lead to more than one target), ux.links.ambiguous{by=context} (the same, counted by name and context together) and ux.links.vague (links whose whole name is a generic phrase, or empty), and fails on an ambiguous name or a vague one. Bind it with radical sense playwright tests/ux/link-texts.spec.ts and the conditions ux.links.ambiguous{by=name} <= 0 and ux.links.vague <= 0. Extend VAGUE with the generic phrases of your language.\n\nThreshold: ux.links.ambiguous{by=name} = 0 and ux.links.vague = 0: on no page of the main journeys does one link name lead to two different targets, and no link is named only \"click here\", \"read more\", \"more\" or the like (or nothing)\n\nTool: Playwright (@playwright/test), measured by radical sense playwright\n\n```ts\n// tests/ux/link-texts.spec.ts: a plain Playwright test (1.50 or later), or measured with\n//   radical sense playwright tests/ux/link-texts.spec.ts\nimport { mkdirSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'\nimport { join } from 'node:path'\nimport { expect, test } from '@playwright/test'\nimport { PAGES } from './journeys'   // the main journeys' pages\n\nconst VAGUE = /^(click here|here|read more|more|learn more|find out more|details|link|this page|continue reading)$/\n\ntype Measurement = { metric: string; value: number; labels?: Record<string, string> }\n/** Writes what the test measured where radical sense playwright reads it; a plain run writes nothing. */\nfunction writeMetrics(file: string, measurements: Measurement[]): void {\n  const dir = process.env.RADICAL_METRICS_DIR\n  if (!dir) return\n  mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true })\n  writeFileSync(join(dir, file), JSON.stringify({ format: 'radical-metrics', version: 1, source: file, at: new Date().toISOString(), measurements }, null, 1))\n}\n\ntest('link names say where they go', async ({ page }) => {\n  const ambiguous = { name: [] as string[], context: [] as string[] }\n  const vague: string[] = []\n  for (const { path } of PAGES) {\n    await page.goto(path)\n    const links = await page.locator('body').evaluate((body) => {\n      const clean = (s: string) => s.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim().toLowerCase()\n      // The accessible name, simplified: aria-labelledby, aria-label, else the text with image alternatives.\n      const nameOf = (a: Element): string => {\n        const ids = a.getAttribute('aria-labelledby')\n        if (ids) return ids.split(/\\s+/).map((id) => document.getElementById(id)?.textContent ?? '').join(' ')\n        const label = a.getAttribute('aria-label')\n        if (label) return label\n        const copy = a.cloneNode(true) as Element\n        copy.querySelectorAll('[aria-hidden=\"true\"]').forEach((el) => el.remove())\n        copy.querySelectorAll('img').forEach((img) => img.replaceWith(img.alt))\n        return copy.textContent ?? ''\n      }\n      return [...body.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement | SVGAElement>('a[href]')].filter((a) => a.checkVisibility()).map((a) => {\n        // an SVG link's href is an SVGAnimatedString (links in diagrams)\n        const url = new URL(a instanceof SVGAElement ? a.href.baseVal : a.href, document.baseURI)\n        // the context: the row the link is in, before the nearest list item, cell, paragraph, definition or card\n        // (closest() alone stops at the cell, and two \"View\" links in one row would never meet)\n        const context = a.closest('tr, [role=\"row\"]') ?? a.closest('li, td, p, dd, article, [role=\"listitem\"]')\n        return { name: clean(nameOf(a)), target: url.origin + url.pathname.replace(/\\/(index\\.html)?$/, '') + url.search, context: clean(context?.textContent ?? '').slice(0, 200) }\n      })\n    })\n    /** The keys that lead to more than one target. */\n    const ambiguousBy = (key: (l: (typeof links)[number]) => string): string[] => {\n      const targets = new Map<string, Set<string>>()\n      for (const l of links) targets.set(key(l), (targets.get(key(l)) ?? new Set<string>()).add(l.target))\n      return [...targets].filter(([, t]) => t.size > 1).map(([k, t]) => `${path}: \"${k}\" leads to ${[...t].join(', ')}`)\n    }\n    ambiguous.name.push(...ambiguousBy((l) => l.name))\n    ambiguous.context.push(...ambiguousBy((l) => `${l.name} in \"${l.context}\"`))\n    vague.push(...links.filter((l) => !l.name || VAGUE.test(l.name)).map((l) => `${path}: \"${l.name}\" to ${l.target}`))\n  }\n  writeMetrics('link-texts.json', [\n    { metric: 'ux.links.ambiguous', value: ambiguous.name.length, labels: { by: 'name' } },\n    { metric: 'ux.links.ambiguous', value: ambiguous.context.length, labels: { by: 'context' } },\n    { metric: 'ux.links.vague', value: vague.length },\n  ])\n  expect.soft(ambiguous.name, 'one link name, several targets').toEqual([])\n  expect.soft(vague, 'link names that say nothing on their own').toEqual([])\n})\n```",
      "hubWhen": {
        "LINK_TEXT": [
          "unique"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ff-link-texts-context",
      "type": "fitness-fn",
      "label": "Link names say where they go",
      "x": 1040,
      "y": 780,
      "characteristic": "interaction-capability",
      "scope": "holistic",
      "cadence": "triggered",
      "trigger": "pull-request",
      "invocation": "automated",
      "description": "A Playwright test opens each page of the main journeys and reads every visible link: its accessible name (simplified: aria-labelledby, aria-label, else its text with image alternatives, aria-hidden parts left out), its target, and its context (the text of the table row around it, else of the nearest list item, cell, paragraph, definition or article, so that two \"View\" links in one row meet). SVG links are read too. It writes ux.links.ambiguous{by=name} (names on a page that lead to more than one target), ux.links.ambiguous{by=context} (the same, counted by name and context together) and ux.links.vague (links whose whole name is a generic phrase, or empty), and fails on a name that is ambiguous within its context. Bind it with radical sense playwright tests/ux/link-texts.spec.ts and the condition ux.links.ambiguous{by=context} <= 0. Extend VAGUE with the generic phrases of your language.\n\nThreshold: ux.links.ambiguous{by=context} = 0: on no page of the main journeys do two links with the same name in the same list item, table row, paragraph or card lead to different targets\n\nTool: Playwright (@playwright/test), measured by radical sense playwright\n\n```ts\n// tests/ux/link-texts.spec.ts: a plain Playwright test (1.50 or later), or measured with\n//   radical sense playwright tests/ux/link-texts.spec.ts\nimport { mkdirSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'\nimport { join } from 'node:path'\nimport { expect, test } from '@playwright/test'\nimport { PAGES } from './journeys'   // the main journeys' pages\n\nconst VAGUE = /^(click here|here|read more|more|learn more|find out more|details|link|this page|continue reading)$/\n\ntype Measurement = { metric: string; value: number; labels?: Record<string, string> }\n/** Writes what the test measured where radical sense playwright reads it; a plain run writes nothing. */\nfunction writeMetrics(file: string, measurements: Measurement[]): void {\n  const dir = process.env.RADICAL_METRICS_DIR\n  if (!dir) return\n  mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true })\n  writeFileSync(join(dir, file), JSON.stringify({ format: 'radical-metrics', version: 1, source: file, at: new Date().toISOString(), measurements }, null, 1))\n}\n\ntest('link names say where they go', async ({ page }) => {\n  const ambiguous = { name: [] as string[], context: [] as string[] }\n  const vague: string[] = []\n  for (const { path } of PAGES) {\n    await page.goto(path)\n    const links = await page.locator('body').evaluate((body) => {\n      const clean = (s: string) => s.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim().toLowerCase()\n      // The accessible name, simplified: aria-labelledby, aria-label, else the text with image alternatives.\n      const nameOf = (a: Element): string => {\n        const ids = a.getAttribute('aria-labelledby')\n        if (ids) return ids.split(/\\s+/).map((id) => document.getElementById(id)?.textContent ?? '').join(' ')\n        const label = a.getAttribute('aria-label')\n        if (label) return label\n        const copy = a.cloneNode(true) as Element\n        copy.querySelectorAll('[aria-hidden=\"true\"]').forEach((el) => el.remove())\n        copy.querySelectorAll('img').forEach((img) => img.replaceWith(img.alt))\n        return copy.textContent ?? ''\n      }\n      return [...body.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement | SVGAElement>('a[href]')].filter((a) => a.checkVisibility()).map((a) => {\n        // an SVG link's href is an SVGAnimatedString (links in diagrams)\n        const url = new URL(a instanceof SVGAElement ? a.href.baseVal : a.href, document.baseURI)\n        // the context: the row the link is in, before the nearest list item, cell, paragraph, definition or card\n        // (closest() alone stops at the cell, and two \"View\" links in one row would never meet)\n        const context = a.closest('tr, [role=\"row\"]') ?? a.closest('li, td, p, dd, article, [role=\"listitem\"]')\n        return { name: clean(nameOf(a)), target: url.origin + url.pathname.replace(/\\/(index\\.html)?$/, '') + url.search, context: clean(context?.textContent ?? '').slice(0, 200) }\n      })\n    })\n    /** The keys that lead to more than one target. */\n    const ambiguousBy = (key: (l: (typeof links)[number]) => string): string[] => {\n      const targets = new Map<string, Set<string>>()\n      for (const l of links) targets.set(key(l), (targets.get(key(l)) ?? new Set<string>()).add(l.target))\n      return [...targets].filter(([, t]) => t.size > 1).map(([k, t]) => `${path}: \"${k}\" leads to ${[...t].join(', ')}`)\n    }\n    ambiguous.name.push(...ambiguousBy((l) => l.name))\n    ambiguous.context.push(...ambiguousBy((l) => `${l.name} in \"${l.context}\"`))\n    vague.push(...links.filter((l) => !l.name || VAGUE.test(l.name)).map((l) => `${path}: \"${l.name}\" to ${l.target}`))\n  }\n  writeMetrics('link-texts.json', [\n    { metric: 'ux.links.ambiguous', value: ambiguous.name.length, labels: { by: 'name' } },\n    { metric: 'ux.links.ambiguous', value: ambiguous.context.length, labels: { by: 'context' } },\n    { metric: 'ux.links.vague', value: vague.length },\n  ])\n  expect.soft(ambiguous.context, 'one link name, several targets in the same context').toEqual([])\n})\n```",
