    {
      "id": "ff-empty-guided",
      "type": "fitness-fn",
      "label": "Empty views explain themselves",
      "x": 1040,
      "y": 1300,
      "characteristic": "interaction-capability",
      "scope": "holistic",
      "cadence": "triggered",
      "trigger": "pull-request",
      "invocation": "automated",
      "description": "A Playwright test signs in as a freshly registered account with no data (a storageState the test setup writes) and opens each view that starts empty (EMPTY_VIEWS in tests/ux/journeys.ts: lists, tables, searches without a result, dashboards). It counts ux.empty.silent, views whose main content shows fewer than three words besides headings and table headers (visible text only, so text hidden for assistive technology or by CSS is not read, and a word has a letter: a lone \"+\" is none), and ux.empty.dead_ends, views without a visible link or button in the main content outside its navigation, and fails on either. Bind it with radical sense playwright tests/ux/empty-states.spec.ts and the conditions ux.empty.silent <= 0 and ux.empty.dead_ends <= 0.\n\nThreshold: ux.empty.silent = 0 and ux.empty.dead_ends = 0: every view that starts empty for a new account says why in at least three words besides its headings, and offers at least one link or button in its main content\n\nTool: Playwright (@playwright/test), measured by radical sense playwright\n\n```ts\n// tests/ux/empty-states.spec.ts: a plain Playwright test (1.50 or later), or measured with\n//   radical sense playwright tests/ux/empty-states.spec.ts\nimport { mkdirSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'\nimport { join } from 'node:path'\nimport { expect, test } from '@playwright/test'\nimport { EMPTY_VIEWS } from './journeys'   // [{ path: '/orders' }, { path: '/search?q=zzzz' }, …]\n\ntest.use({ storageState: 'tests/ux/.auth/new-account.json' })   // a freshly registered account with no data\n\ntype Measurement = { metric: string; value: number; labels?: Record<string, string> }\n/** Writes what the test measured where radical sense playwright reads it; a plain run writes nothing. */\nfunction writeMetrics(file: string, measurements: Measurement[]): void {\n  const dir = process.env.RADICAL_METRICS_DIR\n  if (!dir) return\n  mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true })\n  writeFileSync(join(dir, file), JSON.stringify({ format: 'radical-metrics', version: 1, source: file, at: new Date().toISOString(), measurements }, null, 1))\n}\n\ntest('empty views say why they are empty and what to do next', async ({ page }) => {\n  const silent: string[] = [], deadEnds: string[] = []\n  for (const { path } of EMPTY_VIEWS) {\n    await page.goto(path)\n    const view = await page.getByRole('main').evaluate((main) => {\n      // the words shown besides headings and table headers: visible text only, a word has a letter (\"+\" is none)\n      const skip = 'h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, [role=\"heading\"], th, [role=\"columnheader\"], nav, script, style, [aria-hidden=\"true\"]'\n      const words: string[] = []\n      const walker = document.createTreeWalker(main, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT)\n      for (let text = walker.nextNode(); text; text = walker.nextNode()) {\n        const parent = text.parentElement\n        if (!parent || parent.closest(skip) || !parent.checkVisibility()) continue\n        words.push(...(text.textContent ?? '').split(/\\s+/).filter((w) => /\\p{L}/u.test(w)))\n      }\n      const actions = [...main.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('a[href], button')].filter((x) => !x.closest('nav') && x.checkVisibility())\n      return { words: words.length, actions: actions.length }\n    })\n    if (view.words < 3) silent.push(path)\n    if (!view.actions) deadEnds.push(path)\n  }\n  writeMetrics('empty-states.json', [\n    { metric: 'ux.empty.silent', value: silent.length },\n    { metric: 'ux.empty.dead_ends', value: deadEnds.length },\n  ])\n  expect.soft(silent, 'empty views that say nothing').toEqual([])\n  expect.soft(deadEnds, 'empty views that offer no next step').toEqual([])\n})\n```",
      "hubWhen": {
        "EMPTY": [
          "guided"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ff-empty-plain",
      "type": "fitness-fn",
      "label": "Empty views explain themselves",
      "x": 1040,
      "y": 1430,
      "characteristic": "interaction-capability",
      "scope": "holistic",
      "cadence": "triggered",
      "trigger": "pull-request",
      "invocation": "automated",
      "description": "A Playwright test signs in as a freshly registered account with no data (a storageState the test setup writes) and opens each view that starts empty (EMPTY_VIEWS in tests/ux/journeys.ts: lists, tables, searches without a result, dashboards). It counts ux.empty.silent, views whose main content shows fewer than three words besides headings and table headers (visible text only, so text hidden for assistive technology or by CSS is not read, and a word has a letter: a lone \"+\" is none), and ux.empty.dead_ends, views without a visible link or button in the main content outside its navigation, and fails on a silent view. Bind it with radical sense playwright tests/ux/empty-states.spec.ts and the condition ux.empty.silent <= 0.\n\nThreshold: ux.empty.silent = 0: every view that starts empty for a new account says so in at least three words besides its headings and table headers\n\nTool: Playwright (@playwright/test), measured by radical sense playwright\n\n```ts\n// tests/ux/empty-states.spec.ts: a plain Playwright test (1.50 or later), or measured with\n//   radical sense playwright tests/ux/empty-states.spec.ts\nimport { mkdirSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'\nimport { join } from 'node:path'\nimport { expect, test } from '@playwright/test'\nimport { EMPTY_VIEWS } from './journeys'   // [{ path: '/orders' }, { path: '/search?q=zzzz' }, …]\n\ntest.use({ storageState: 'tests/ux/.auth/new-account.json' })   // a freshly registered account with no data\n\ntype Measurement = { metric: string; value: number; labels?: Record<string, string> }\n/** Writes what the test measured where radical sense playwright reads it; a plain run writes nothing. */\nfunction writeMetrics(file: string, measurements: Measurement[]): void {\n  const dir = process.env.RADICAL_METRICS_DIR\n  if (!dir) return\n  mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true })\n  writeFileSync(join(dir, file), JSON.stringify({ format: 'radical-metrics', version: 1, source: file, at: new Date().toISOString(), measurements }, null, 1))\n}\n\ntest('empty views say why they are empty', async ({ page }) => {\n  const silent: string[] = [], deadEnds: string[] = []\n  for (const { path } of EMPTY_VIEWS) {\n    await page.goto(path)\n    const view = await page.getByRole('main').evaluate((main) => {\n      // the words shown besides headings and table headers: visible text only, a word has a letter (\"+\" is none)\n      const skip = 'h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6, [role=\"heading\"], th, [role=\"columnheader\"], nav, script, style, [aria-hidden=\"true\"]'\n      const words: string[] = []\n      const walker = document.createTreeWalker(main, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT)\n      for (let text = walker.nextNode(); text; text = walker.nextNode()) {\n        const parent = text.parentElement\n        if (!parent || parent.closest(skip) || !parent.checkVisibility()) continue\n        words.push(...(text.textContent ?? '').split(/\\s+/).filter((w) => /\\p{L}/u.test(w)))\n      }\n      const actions = [...main.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('a[href], button')].filter((x) => !x.closest('nav') && x.checkVisibility())\n      return { words: words.length, actions: actions.length }\n    })\n    if (view.words < 3) silent.push(path)\n    if (!view.actions) deadEnds.push(path)\n  }\n  writeMetrics('empty-states.json', [\n    { metric: 'ux.empty.silent', value: silent.length },\n    { metric: 'ux.empty.dead_ends', value: deadEnds.length },\n  ])\n  expect.soft(silent, 'empty views that say nothing').toEqual([])\n})\n```",
      "hubWhen": {
        "EMPTY": [
          "plain"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ff-heuristic-review",
      "type": "fitness-fn",
      "label": "Heuristic review held and acted on",
      "x": 1040,
      "y": 1560,
      "characteristic": "interaction-capability",
      "scope": "holistic",
      "cadence": "temporal",
      "every": "{{REVIEW_DAYS}}d",
      "invocation": "manual",
      "description": "Every {{REVIEW_DAYS}} days, and before each major release, three people (a designer, a developer and someone who knows the users' work; not the authors of the screens alone) each walk the main journeys alone against the heuristics and principles below, then merge their findings, rate each on Nielsen's severity scale (the mean of the three ratings) and file an issue for every finding rated 3 or 4. The record is committed under docs/usability/reviews/, one file per review, named by its date; the release checklist asks for the latest record and for its 3s and 4s to be closed.\n\nThreshold: A review record no older than {{REVIEW_DAYS}} days (and one since the last major release), from three evaluators, with every finding rated; 0 findings rated 3 or 4 open at a release\n\nTool: A review record in the repository (Markdown), three evaluators\n\n```md\n<!-- docs/usability/reviews/2026-11-24.md: one file per review; the next is due {{REVIEW_DAYS}} days later -->\n# Heuristic review, 2026-11-24\n\nBuild reviewed: v1.8.0 (commit abc1234)\nJourneys: sign up, place an order, change the delivery address\nEvaluators, each alone first: A. Designer, B. Developer, C. Support lead\n\n| No. | Where (page, step) | Heuristic or principle | What happens | Severity (mean of 3) | Issue | Fixed in |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | /checkout, address | H5 Error prevention; ISO: use error robustness | A typo in the postcode is found only after payment | 3 | #412 | |\n| 2 | /orders | H1 Visibility of system status | The list shows nothing while it loads | 2 | #413 | |\n\nHeuristics (Nielsen): H1 Visibility of system status; H2 Match between the system and the real world; H3 User control and freedom; H4 Consistency and standards; H5 Error prevention; H6 Recognition rather than recall; H7 Flexibility and efficiency of use; H8 Aesthetic and minimalist design; H9 Help users recognize, diagnose, and recover from errors; H10 Help and documentation.\nPrinciples (ISO 9241-110:2020): suitability for the user's tasks; self-descriptiveness; conformity with user expectations; learnability; controllability; use error robustness; user engagement.\nSeverity (Nielsen): 0 not a problem, 1 cosmetic, 2 minor, 3 major (fix before the release), 4 catastrophe (fix before the release).\nOutcome: findings rated 3 or 4: 1, all with an issue; release blocked until #412 is closed.\n```"
    }
  ],
  "relations": [
    {
      "id": "req-nav-shared--derives--need",
      "sourceId": "req-nav-shared",
      "targetId": "need",
      "relationType": "derives",
      "quote": "People use this front end to get their tasks done, most without training. They must find their way with navigation that stays the same from page to page, links that are neither repeated nor vague (not the same link five times on one page, not five links named \"Read more\"), forms that say what went wrong and where, and empty views that say why they are empty; and the usability of the whole must be reviewed against recognised principles on a schedule, not only after users complain. The checks assume Playwright tests under tests/ux with tests/ux/journeys.ts listing the main journeys' pages in the order a user walks them (PAGES: path, and the section where sections have their own navigation), their forms (FORMS: path, the submit button's name, the label of one field with a format to check) and the views that start empty for a new account (EMPTY_VIEWS: path); playwright.config sets the baseURL and, for pages behind sign-in, a storageState. Each test fails on its own in a plain run and, run by radical sense playwright, writes what it measured as a radical-metrics/1 file into RADICAL_METRICS_DIR."
    },
    {
      "id": "req-nav-sections--derives--need",
      "sourceId": "req-nav-sections",
      "targetId": "need",
      "relationType": "derives",
      "quote": "People use this front end to get their tasks done, most without training. They must find their way with navigation that stays the same from page to page, links that are neither repeated nor vague (not the same link five times on one page, not five links named \"Read more\"), forms that say what went wrong and where, and empty views that say why they are empty; and the usability of the whole must be reviewed against recognised principles on a schedule, not only after users complain. The checks assume Playwright tests under tests/ux with tests/ux/journeys.ts listing the main journeys' pages in the order a user walks them (PAGES: path, and the section where sections have their own navigation), their forms (FORMS: path, the submit button's name, the label of one field with a format to check) and the views that start empty for a new account (EMPTY_VIEWS: path); playwright.config sets the baseURL and, for pages behind sign-in, a storageState. Each test fails on its own in a plain run and, run by radical sense playwright, writes what it measured as a radical-metrics/1 file into RADICAL_METRICS_DIR."
    },
